Subject: [PARKED reference] AVLO: 0008 snapshot half — getExpectedKeys 5-entry table

PARKED until P2 (redesign P1 deviation 1). This was the snapshot-capture
half of 0008 against pyodide 0.29.4 — kept as the empirical record of the
post-0008 hiwire layout, NOT applied by build.sh (parked/ is outside the
patch glob). P2's owned capture re-derives the expected-keys slots
empirically against 314 (the layout is boot-allocation-ordered and will
differ); do not apply this diff verbatim.

Original rationale (0.29.4): getExpectedKeys() hardcodes the first hiwire
regular-table entries in boot allocation order, and the "js" registration
(deleted by 0008's surviving api.ts hunk) was what interned jsglobals
(slot 1) plus a trailing {} (slot 6). Post-0008 the table is
[null, public_api, API, scheduleCallback, API] (verified empirically,
stable across warmups+gc) — without this update makeSnapshot's checkEntry
dies stringifying public_api (circular Module.FS root) against the stale
jsglobals expectation. Capture and restore share the list; BUILD_ID
gating rejects pre-0008 snapshots.

